Andrew,

please check the below meeting minutes with Hellmann.
I want to make sure I don=92t write something we didn=92t talk about.

Thanks a lot. :)



TO : UCG, ASM, WCG
CC : SSC, CCA, CCB, CCM, ASG, WSG
FM : CCE

We had a meeting with Hellmann on 19th NOV at SEL H/O.
Please kindly refer to the meeting minutes with Hellmann as following.



1.    Attendees



-. Hellmann Worldwide Logistics

Mr. Jens Pottschul, VP, Sefreight Asia

Mr. Oliver Nicolaysen, VP Seafreight OMEA

Mr. Monar Yoo, VP, Hellmann Korea Ocean Freight Dept.

Mr. IH Moon, G.Manager, Hellmann Korea Ocean Freight Dept.



-. HJS

CCA =96 Sang-Young SHIN, Ho-Sik PARK, Alex SONG

CCE =96 Sang-Jin HAN, Woo-Jung KIM, Luth(Kyung-Won) CHOI

CCB =96 Sylvia(He-Jung) KIM





2.    Opening



1) Overall atmosphere was very friendly and the positive discussion was exc=
hanged.

-. Hellmann is very satisfied with our service and expressed their willingn=
ess to grow together.



2) Hellmann gave the brief presentation about the company.

-. It has 443 branches in 158 countries and its total ocean volume is 578,0=
00TEU in 2012.

-. Hellmann is comparatively younger than other international F/FWD in inte=
rnational biz wise.

-. Hellmann had been strong at Airfreight but started to develop more ocean=
 biz since 8-9 years ago.

--> Seafreight sector is growing faster than inland and airfreight biz.

-. Totally 12 core carriers and their volume is almost 81% of total volume

--> With core carriers, Hellmann is trying to penetrate all trade lanes.

-. Currently AES biz is very developed, but Hellmann wants expand more biz =
with the global perspective.



3) HJS gave the brief presentation regarding HJS organization change.

-. Introduced customer group and Hellmann was very interested in our new or=
ganization change.





3.    TPS E/B & LATAM Discussion



-. Satisfied with our services, but requested more competitive pricing for =
the biz development.

-. Agreed to grow together in 2014 and closely communicate

-. TPSE MQC for 2014 will be set up as 4,000TEU. (Same as 2013.)

-. Hellmann is one of Top5 NVO in Mexico and trying to expand the biz in LA=
TAM.(recently 36% increase)

-. The total volume in LATAM is 30,000TEU.

-. The LATAM markets where Hellmann is focusing are Mexico, Brazil, and Arg=
entina.

-. Brazil is the one of strategic country to develop and Argentina is also =
very important.

-. Even though current biz status is small, agreed to develop more in LATAM=
 ex Asia.





4.    IAS Discussion



-. Intra-Asia market is changing very fast so that rate should be tuned in =
the market.

--> But, HJS rate is not good enough and requested to be more aggressive.

-. Rate level as well as response time are two major factors for the succes=
sful biz.

-. M.East market is one of the fastest growing markets(61% increase) for He=
llmann,

but not much support from HJS so far.

-. Hellmann already have offices in Dubai and Kuwait, and Hellmann Saudi Ar=
abia will be

open on 1st DEC and now look into Qatar.

--> There will be more to come and they need support from HJS.

-. For AADA area(ex Asia South bound), 1,000TEU in 2014 is set for the targ=
et.

-. HJS will provide the reasonable pricing after the close market monitorin=
g for AU biz.

-. Request more New Zealand shipment, but Hellmann is also having a difficu=
lty in New Zealand

as there are not much potential to develop. However, they will consider it =
positively.

-. Not much volume out of M.East to F.E.Asia as the market itself is not bi=
g enough.

-. Agree to exchange the potential area to develop together in Intra-Asia.

--> HJS will try to provide more competitive rate for those areas.





5.    Next Step



-. Already set up the focal point in SHAAS and SINWA for the better communi=
cation about IAS.

-. Will study how to communicate with Hellmann regarding faster rate update=
 for IAS.

-. CCE will review Hellmann=92s global target for 2014 within this week.



Thanks&B.Rgds
WJ Kim

